  CharacterPrefab: {fileID: 2426892980417719112, guid: f6bc53fd6529ba64dbccf80b57f37fa7, type: 3}
  entryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - Returning to my registered residence.
    - Completing the evening census route.
    - Resident returning home before sunset.
    midDaysReasons:
    - Updating the local registry. Some records need correcting.
    - Delivering documentation to the district office.
    - Returning to my apartment. I do not stay out long.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - All remaining residents must be accounted for. I am one of them.
    - The records need to be current. I make sure of that.
    - Going home. The door is always unlocked for me.
  invalidEntryReasons:
    earlyDaysReasons:
    - I need to see the names on this checkpoint's registry.
    - Someone at this post is not in my records.
    - I was waiting outside until the right person came on shift.
    midDaysReasons:
    - There are names in the registry that should not be here.
    - I am collecting the last known addresses of the recently departed.
    - I need access to the eastern ward's mortality files.
    finalDaysReasons:
    - Some residents have not been recorded correctly. I will fix that.
    - I am here to close certain files.
    - One of the names on the list is already gone. I wanted to confirm it in person.
  entryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Good evening. Here are my documents. Everything is in order, as always.
    - I have all the correct papers. I filed them myself.
    - You are new here. I know the names of everyone who has worked this post.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - The registry has some gaps now. That happens in situations like this. I fill
      them.
    - I keep very careful records. It helps to know who is left.
    - Do not worry. I have been through this checkpoint thirty-one times. I know
      the procedure.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - I counted every checkpoint visit from the beginning. You will want to record
      that.
    - I always know when something is ending. It is a useful skill.
    - Everything in my file is accurate. I double-check.
  uncannyEntryDialogues:
    lastVerdict: 0
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - 
    - 
    - 
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - 
    - 
    - 
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - 
    - 
    - 
  exitDialoguesPassed:
    lastVerdict: 1
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - Wonderful. Goodbye. I will remember your face.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - Of course. I knew you would let me through.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - Thank you. The records appreciate your cooperation.
  exitDialoguesQuarantined:
    lastVerdict: 2
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - That is fine. I will update my own file accordingly.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - May I have a pencil? I keep notes.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - I expected this. I noted the date and time already.
  exitDialoguesKilled:
    lastVerdict: 3
    dialoguesEarlyDays:
    - I see. I will need a moment to update my records.
    dialoguesMidDays:
    - I had already written this down. I hope that does not trouble you.
    dialoguesFinalDays:
    - It is only a name. Names go into the registry. Everything does, eventually.
  quarantineExitLines:
  - I will need writing materials. I have twelve entries still pending.
  - I always behave. It is the people around me who change.
  - I knew a woman who was quarantined here once. She is not in the records anymore.
  killExitLines:
  - I updated my own entry this morning. Just in case. It was accurate.
  - The record outlasts the person. That is the point of a record.
  - I knew the name of the last person who stood here. Now I will know yours.
  voiceAudioClips:
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 03a2801751dcbdc41ae67384569e0a84, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 339c0ab6ad5f84d46bf06f5892c9d2f9, type: 3}
  - {fileID: 8300000, guid: 96aaf0a0f9777954db2cbe9a6e504c85, type: 3}
